==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|desplacer|lang=frm}} (French: {{term/t|fr|déplacer}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪsˈpleɪs/|/dɪzˈpleɪs/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/dɪsˈpleɪs/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪs}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|displac|ing}}

# To [[move]] something, or someone, especially to [[forcibly]] move [[people]] from their [[homeland]].
# To [[supplant]], or take the place of something or someone; to [[substitute]].
# {{context|of a floating ship|lang=en}} To have a [[weight]] equal to that of the [[water]] displaced.

